name: conformance-std-aggregator-approx
version: 1.0.0
known-red: "js, jvm — two independent, filed codegen bugs, one per lane (int's own two bugs — missing math.log, lexicographic sortBy on a Double key — are fixed, see v1/runtime/backend/interpreter/BUGS.md). js: HLLAgg's hash mixer needs Array.fill/List.tabulate with a bit-shifted Int count, and the JS backend's Array.fill/List.fill/*.tabulate reject a BigInt count with TypeError: Cannot convert a BigInt value to a number (v1/runtime/backend/js/BUGS.md js-codegen-array-fill-and-tabulate-reject-a-bigint-count). jvm: run-jvm transpiles a 64-bit Long literal (fmix64's mixing constants) into a context requiring a 32-bit Int, a symptom of the pre-existing, already-tracked int-width non-conformance (see int-width's own known-red). CMSMonoid alone is unaffected and correct on every lane. EXPIRES when both remaining bugs are fixed."
---

# Std — Approximate Aggregators (HyperLogLog, Count-Min Sketch, T-Digest)

Exercises §6 of [`specs/aggregation-algebra.md`](../../specs/aggregation-algebra.md): sketches that
are `Monoid`s trading exactness for a bounded error at fixed memory.

[Aggregator, runAggregator, strHash, HLLAgg, CMSMonoid, TDigestMonoid](std/aggregator.ssc)

```scalascript
val hll  = HLLAgg[String](12, s => strHash(17, s))
val keys = (1 to 10000).toList.map(i => "item-" + i.toString)
println(runAggregator(keys, hll))
println(hll.errorBound)

var partA = hll.monoid.empty
for k <- (1 to 3000).toList.map(i => "merge-" + i.toString) do partA = hll.monoid.combine(partA, hll.prepare(k))
var partB = hll.monoid.empty
for k <- (2500 to 6000).toList.map(i => "merge-" + i.toString) do partB = hll.monoid.combine(partB, hll.prepare(k))
println(hll.present(hll.monoid.combine(partA, partB)))

val cms = CMSMonoid(4, 64)
var cacc = cms.empty
cacc = cms.add(cacc, "apple")
cacc = cms.add(cacc, "apple")
cacc = cms.add(cacc, "apple")
cacc = cms.add(cacc, "banana")
cacc = cms.add(cacc, "banana")
cacc = cms.add(cacc, "cherry")
println(cms.estimate(cacc, "apple"))
println(cms.estimate(cacc, "banana"))
println(cms.estimate(cacc, "cherry"))
println(cms.estimate(cacc, "durian"))

val td = TDigestMonoid(20)
var d1 = td.empty
for i <- 1 to 100 do d1 = td.addPoint(d1, i.toDouble)
var d2 = td.empty
for i <- 101 to 200 do d2 = td.addPoint(d2, i.toDouble)
val combined = td.combine(d1, d2)
println(combined.centroids.length)
println(td.quantile(combined, 0.5))
println(td.quantile(combined, 0.99))
```
